// jet_builtins — Core's one door to the compiler.
//
// This module declares what the compiler itself provides to Core: its kernel
// operations, the storage types those operations work on, and the markers
// only the compiler can honor. A name here drops the `__` it carried in the
// module it left.
//
// A Core module reaches the compiler through `use builtin: jet_builtins` and
// a `builtin.` path, so reading Core shows each place the compiler acts. Only
// Core sources import this module; any other program gets E1013 and reaches
// the same operations through Core's public modules.
//
// A Core item the compiler names belongs here. Tests/Guards/core_builtins_door.jet
// counts the compiler-known names Core still declares in other modules, and
// that count only falls.
//
// An operation the host runs has no declaration here: its row in
// Compiler/Prelude/Core.rows (`dispatcher_row … jet_builtins <name>`) and its
// typed signature in the compiler's host signature table are the whole
// operation. This file declares the records those operations return.

// The roles a Core function fills for the compiler: `abs` on a Float
// (AbsFloat), an F32 (AbsF32) and an I64 (AbsI64), `pow` on a Float
// (PowFloat) and an F32 (PowF32), the zero test of a Fraction divisor
// (FractionIsZero) and the Fraction an Int `/` (FractionFromParts) and a
// Fraction `/` (FractionDiv) make once that test passes, a fallible unit
// conversion's exact check (UnitConversionExact) and its rounded one
// (UnitConversionRounded), the text inputs keeping an `on_drop:`
// (TextInputDrop) and an `on_change:` (TextInputChange) handler's slot, the
// constructors of a declared point, an `Event<T>` (EventPoint), a
// `Hook<T, R>` (HookPoint) and a `DecisionHook<T, E>` (DecisionPoint), each
// call a binding's identity rather than an allocation, the line readers
// `loop line in child.stdout.lines()` calls for each line of a child's
// output (ProcessStdoutLine) and error output (ProcessStderrLine), and the
// decode helpers a `tree.decode<T>()` with no Decode implementation of T's
// own runs for a List (DecodeList), a `[T#N]` (DecodeFixedList), a byte List
// (DecodeBytes), an Option (DecodeOption) and a String-keyed Map
// (DecodeMap), with the one `FieldError.under` runs (DecodeUnder). The
// `core.units` helpers a `Measurement<Float>` runs fill roles too: making one
// from a value and its uncertainty (MeasurementNew), its `.value`
// (MeasurementValue) and `.uncertainty` (MeasurementUncertainty), its `+`,
// `-`, `*` and `/` (MeasurementAdd, MeasurementSub, MeasurementMul,
// MeasurementDiv), its `math.sqrt` (MeasurementSqrt), its text
// (MeasurementShow) and a rounded conversion into a measured unit
// (MeasurementResult). The `core.compute` helpers a Tensor range runs fill
// roles too: the flat slab range a window views (TensorWindow) and the
// Tensor its `.copy()` makes (TensorWindowCopy), as do the autodiff tape
// calls of a transform: entering (TapeEnter) and leaving (TapeExit) the
// tape, making a leaf (TapeLeaf), the untracked value (TapeValue), a
// gradient (TapeGradient), a `vjp` pullback (TapePull) and a `jvp` tangent
// (TapeTangent). The `core.data` helpers a checked query runs fill roles
// too: the `Query` stages `filter` (QueryFilter), `sort_by` (QuerySortBy),
// `map` (QueryMap), `min` (QueryMin), `max` (QueryMax), `inner_join`
// (QueryInnerJoin), `left_join` (QueryLeftJoin), `collect` (QueryCollect)
// and `group_by` (QueryGroupBy), a query over a tracked
// source (QueryTracked) or a stream (QueryStream), a grouped `count`
// (GroupCount), `mean` (GroupMean) and `sum` by its value's numeric type
// (GroupSumInt, GroupSumFloat, GroupSumF32, GroupSumI8 through GroupSumI64,
// GroupSumU8 through GroupSumU64), the event-time stages `with_event_time`
// by an `Int` (StreamWithEventTime) or a `DateTime` (StreamWithEventDatetime)
// stamp, `key_by` (StreamKeyBy) and `window` (StreamWindow), and
// `data.schema` (DataSchema). The source functions other Core calls forward
// to fill roles too: a list's SQL `query` (ListQuery), a typed
// `json.decode<T>` (JSONTypedDecode), `toml.decode<T>` (TOMLTypedDecode) and
// `yaml.decode<T>` (YAMLTypedDecode), a `JobQueue`'s `enqueue` (JobEnqueue)
// and `delay` (JobDelay), a service's `app.enqueue` (AppEnqueue),
// `net.unix_connect` without (UnixConnect) and with a deadline
// (UnixConnectDeadline), `tls.client` over a stream (TLSClientStream), with a
// deadline (TLSClientDeadline) and with a config and a deadline
// (TLSClientConfigDeadline), and `term.take` (TermTake). The `#CLI` entry the
// compiler generates calls the core.args parser helpers by their roles, each
// starting with `CLI` (CLISpec through CLIMissing), whose fillers the compiler
// reads from Core/Args/Args.jet while it builds. `context.allocator` reads
// the function that fills ContextAllocator, and a `#Context(allocator: a)`
// block calls the one that fills AllocatorHandler on `a`. The core.mem and
// core.math operations the compiler builds inline at each call, never as a
// call (a raw List's capacity, a pointer step, a block copy, a bit copy and
// the rest), fill the roles that start with `Inline`. A role's name ends
// in `Point` exactly when it is a point constructor's, starts with `Decode`
// exactly when it is a decode helper's, starts with `Inline` exactly when it
// is a builder intrinsic's, starts with `Measurement` exactly when it is a
// measurement helper's, and starts with `Tape` exactly when it is an
// autodiff tape call's.
// The compiler runs the one Core function that fills a role and never names
// it, so the function can be private and keep any name.
// The rest are filled by a trait of Compiler/Prelude/Traits.jet, whose
// `#Builtin.Role(.Add)` line gives it the role: the trait `a + b` (Add),
// `a - b` (Sub), `a * b` (Mul) and `a / b` (Div) call, the one `==` and `!=`
// call (Equal), the one `<=>`, `<`, `>`, `<=` and `>=` call (Compare), and
// the ones `a[k]` (Index) and `a[k] = v` (IndexMut) call. A library type
// takes an operator by implementing the trait, which the compiler finds
// through its role, never through its name.
// Each role is filled exactly once (E1014 for a second filler; E1015 when
// `jet check Core` finds one unfilled). Tools/Agent/OwnedTraitRows.jet writes
// the cases from the `#Builtin.Role(.X)` markers: the Core functions' by path
// and line, then the traits'. Tests/UI/CoreRole* put a probe after
// `RoleKind: enum {`.
// BEGIN GENERATED by Tools/Agent/OwnedTraitRows.jet from the `#Builtin.Role(.X)` markers; do not edit.
RoleKind: enum {
    LiveBind,
    LivePoll,
    LivePush,
    LiveInvalidate,
    LiveInvalidateAll,
    LiveArg,
    AppEnqueue,
    CLISpec,
    CLIIsInt,
    CLIIsFloat,
    CLIIsBool,
    CLIUnknown,
    CLIParse,
    CLIParseFloat,
    CLIStatus,
    CLIMessage,
    CLICommandName,
    CLIFlag,
    CLIExplicit,
    CLIValue,
    CLITextOf,
    CLIIntOf,
    CLIFloatOf,
    CLIBoolOf,
    CLITextOptOf,
    CLIIntOptOf,
    CLIFloatOptOf,
    CLIBoolOptOf,
    CLIArgv,
    CLIUsage,
    CLIWithUsage,
    CLILong,
    CLIShort,
    CLIRest,
    CLISlice,
    CLIEq,
    CLIIntRefusal,
    CLIFloatRefusal,
    CLIChoiceRefusal,
    CLIFlagValue,
    CLISurplus,
    CLIMissing,
    TensorWindow,
    TensorWindowCopy,
    TapeEnter,
    TapeExit,
    TapeLeaf,
    TapeValue,
    TapeGradient,
    TapePull,
    TapeTangent,
    ListQuery,
    QueryStream,
    StreamWithEventTime,
    StreamWithEventDatetime,
    QueryTracked,
    QueryCollect,
    QueryFilter,
    QuerySortBy,
    QueryMap,
    QueryMin,
    QueryMax,
    QueryInnerJoin,
    QueryLeftJoin,
    QueryGroupBy,
    GroupCount,
    GroupSumInt,
    GroupSumFloat,
    GroupSumF32,
    GroupSumI8,
    GroupSumI16,
    GroupSumI32,
    GroupSumI64,
    GroupSumU8,
    GroupSumU16,
    GroupSumU32,
    GroupSumU64,
    GroupMean,
    DataSchema,
    DecodeUnder,
    DecodeList,
    DecodeFixedList,
    DecodeBytes,
    DecodeOption,
    DecodeMap,
    JSONTypedDecode,
    TOMLTypedDecode,
    YAMLTypedDecode,
    EventPoint,
    HookPoint,
    DecisionPoint,
    JobEnqueue,
    JobDelay,
    AbsFloat,
    PowFloat,
    PowF32,
    AbsF32,
    AbsI64,
    InlineFloatBits,
    InlineFloatFromBits,
    FractionFromParts,
    FractionDiv,
    FractionIsZero,
    UnitConversionExact,
    UnitConversionRounded,
    InlineVolatileRead,
    InlineVolatileWrite,
    InlineMemCopy,
    InlineMemFill,
    InlineListAppend,
    InlineListCopy,
    InlineAllocRaw,
    InlineFreeRaw,
    InlineMapped,
    InlineUnmapping,
    InlineViewFromRaw,
    InlineStreamStore,
    InlineTypeSize,
    InlineListCapacity,
    InlineListReserveExact,
    InlinePtrOffset,
    InlinePtrByteOffset,
    InlineRegionReserve,
    InlineRegionRelease,
    AllocatorHandler,
    InlineContextTake,
    InlineContextGive,
    InlineContextRoom,
    ContextAllocator,
    UnixConnect,
    UnixConnectDeadline,
    TLSClientStream,
    TLSClientDeadline,
    TLSClientConfigDeadline,
    ProcessStdoutLine,
    ProcessStderrLine,
    StringMatches,
    StringMatch,
    StringHasLine,
    TermTake,
    StringTrimNewlines,
    StringFirstLines,
    StringLastLines,
    StringHasLinePrefix,
    StringTSVRecords,
    StringCompareVersion,
    TextInputDrop,
    TextInputChange,
    MeasurementNew,
    MeasurementValue,
    MeasurementUncertainty,
    MeasurementAdd,
    MeasurementSub,
    MeasurementMul,
    MeasurementDiv,
    MeasurementSqrt,
    MeasurementShow,
    MeasurementResult,
    Add,
    Sub,
    Mul,
    Div,
    Equal,
    Compare,
    Index,
    IndexMut,
}
// END GENERATED

// `#Builtin.Role(.X)` on a Core function makes it the one that fills role X.
Role: struct {
    kind: RoleKind,

    impl Marker {
        sites: [.Function],
    }
}

// The storage of the number families: a machine word of
// `bits` bits, which `Signed<bits>` and `Unsigned<bits>` in the prelude
// hold, and an IEEE 754 binary float with `exponent` exponent bits and
// `fraction` fraction bits, which `IEEE<exponent, fraction>` holds. A
// standard size of a family is the compiler's own number type for it
// (`Unsigned<8>` is U8), so no value of these two is built.
Word: struct<bits: Int> {}

FloatWord: struct<exponent: Int, fraction: Int> {}

// The test harness's evidence and temporary-directory operations
// (`core.testing`'s snap, golden, fixture and temp_dir): plain records of
// physical facts, not raw-codec tuples.

// `evidence_read(path)`: a snapshot, golden or fixture file's text.
EvidenceRead: struct {
    ok: Bool,
    text: String,
    missing: Bool,
}

// `temp_facts()`: the process and thread a temporary directory is named for.
TempFacts: struct {
    pid: U64,
    thread: String,
}

// `temp_join(name)`: a path under the temporary root. `path` is the host's
// opaque platform encoding of it: pass it back to temp_remove and
// temp_create unchanged, never built, sliced, decoded or edited. `text` is
// its lossy display form.
TempPath: struct {
    path: [U8],
    text: String,
}

// `temp_remove(path)`: whether the old directory is gone.
TempRemove: struct {
    ok: Bool,
    missing: Bool,
    cause: String,
}

// `temp_create(path)`: whether the new directory exists.
TempCreate: struct {
    ok: Bool,
    cause: String,
}

// The descriptor operations core.files.sealed reads and writes files through
// (jetc_open_directory, jetc_read, jetc_link and the rest): whole-record
// physical facts of one system call.

// What every descriptor operation but jetc_stat returns. `value` is the
// descriptor or byte count, negative on failure with `errno` set; `bytes`
// is what jetc_read read. `linux` is a compile-time host capability,
// consumed once at parent open.
JetcRaw: struct {
    value: Int,
    errno: Int,
    bytes: [U8],
    linux: Bool,
}

// `jetc_stat(fd)`: an open descriptor's metadata, `status` negative on
// failure with `errno` set.
JetcStat: struct {
    status: Int,
    errno: Int,
    dev: Int,
    ino: Int,
    len: Int,
    mtime: Int,
    mtime_ns: Int,
    nlink: Int,
    is_file: Bool,
    is_dir: Bool,
}

// The advisory-lock operations core.files' lock and try_lock run on
// (lock_open, lock_try, lock_wait, lock_close, lock_fd_identity,
// lock_path_identity and lock_owner): plain records of the host's facts.
// `errno` and `platform` are the host's own error numbers, which core.files
// maps to IOError.

// What lock_open and lock_try return: `value` is the descriptor or result,
// negative on failure.
LockCall: struct {
    value: Int,
    errno: Int,
    platform: Int,
}

// What lock_fd_identity and lock_path_identity return: the file a descriptor
// or path names, so a replaced lock file is told apart from the held one.
LockIdentity: struct {
    device: Int,
    low: Int,
    high: Int,
    regular: Bool,
    reparse: Bool,
    errno: Int,
    platform: Int,
}

// What lock_wait returns: whether the lock was taken before `deadline_ns`.
LockWait: struct {
    acquired: Bool,
    timed_out: Bool,
    errno: Int,
    platform: Int,
    deadline_ns: Int,
}

// `resolve_ordered(host, port)`: core.net's name resolution. It answers
// every address in the platform's order, or this failure: `kind` is the
// failure class core.net maps to a NetError, and `os_code` counts only when
// `has_os_code` is set.
ResolveError: struct {
    kind: Int,
    has_os_code: Bool,
    os_code: Int,
    message: String,
}

// The operation an `IOContext` failed in. It stays a payload-free runtime
// `Copy` enum, and only Core source may name it in an annotation.
IOOperation: enum {
    Read,
    Write,
    Flush,
    Connect,
    Accept,
    Close,
    Resolve,
    Codec,
}

// The limit a process or pipeline ran out of, the payload of
// `IOError.ResourceLimit` and a receipt's `limit_hit`. The runtime builds it
// by its position (jet.runtime.process).
ProcessResourceLimit: enum {
    WallTime,
    CPUTime,
    Memory,
    OpenFiles,
    Output,
}

// The file steps of an upload endpoint (core.app's uploads). core.web asks
// for a step by handing core.app's `FileJob` to the lambda the compiler
// writes where the endpoint's service is mounted, and that lambda runs it, so
// only a program that mounts the service reaches its files and stores. The
// server streams an admitted request's body to a staged file as it reads it:
// `Open` stages an empty file, each `Write` appends the next bytes to the
// staged file it names, and `Abandon` removes one whose request ended before
// its body did. `Claim` hands a staged file to the request this task
// answers. The other steps end that request, answer a blob's GET by its id,
// or remove what a server that stopped left staged, as a server starts.
FileStep: enum {
    Open,
    Write(name: String, piece: [U8]),
    Abandon(String),
    Claim(String),
    Finish,
    Serve(String),
    Clean,
}

// What a file step gave: its status, 200 when it did what it was asked;
// for a blob's GET, the blob's bytes and their content type; the name of
// the file `Open` staged; and the size of the file `Claim` handed over.
FileDone: struct {
    status: Int,
    body: [U8],
    media: String,
    staged: String{""},
    bytes: Int{0},
}
